-- `exports_ignored` (boundary.md §5.2, amended 2026-10-20): this project
-- lists a name under `"exports"`, but its platform — `plain`, layered on
-- `node` and declaring nothing of its own — declares no `"exports"`, so
-- the list does nothing. A list that does nothing is almost always a
-- mistake, so it is a warning (CLAUDE.md rule 7) and the build goes on;
-- the `.diag` golden pins it. The platform directory is here so that the
-- harness copies the whole project, `beni.json` included.
import Node exposing (Program)


main : Program
main = Node.print "built anyway"
